---
arrangement: why-reason-run-not-elidable
when-used: The ANALYSIS row for a site that ran for none of the more specific reasons.
why: The residual arm: a mutator with no converged report, an inert builtin, or a running wall above it. Named as a set because the render cannot yet say which member applies.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- why-reason-run-not-elidable && mise run loom:promote -- why-reason-run-not-elidable`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all why-reason-run-not-elidable` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# `cd` is a no-target-state builtin: no read-only check could ever be authored for it, so the
# firehose deliberately says nothing about it (cheap-7) and the addressed answer is the quiet one.
cd /var/tmp
hork tune --profile web

-- replay --
